        "type": "Module",
        "name": "preamp_stage",
        "description": "NE5532 dual operational amplifier used as the low-level preamplifier domain for the compact audio amplifier. This module accepts the external audio input, applies the primary voltage gain needed to reach the overall target gain range when combined with the downstream LM386 stage, and drives the LM386 input with an analog signal output. The device operates directly from the single VIN_9V supply and GND, so downstream wiring must implement an appropriate single-supply input and feedback biasing scheme around the used amplifier channel. Only one amplifier channel is required by the brief; the second NE5532 channel is uncommitted and should remain intentionally parked in a defined state during detailed design rather than left floating. This module is responsible for the low-level analog signal path and should keep its feedback and bias network local, with return-current routing planned to minimize coupling from the speaker current path.",
        "id": "preamp_stage"
      },
