      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_amp_stage",
        "description": "LM386 low-voltage audio power amplifier used as the final power output stage. This module receives the low-level analog drive from the NE5532 preamplifier, provides the final voltage and power gain needed to drive an 8-ohm speaker from the single VIN_9V supply, and exposes the amplified speaker output as the board-level load interface. The LM386 operates from VIN_9V and GND. Its gain-setting intent depends on the network between GAIN_1 and GAIN_2, which must be selected in detailed design so that the combined NE5532 plus LM386 chain lands in the requested overall gain range of about 100x to 200x; this gain is not assumed internally. IN_NEG should be configured per the intended single-ended application during downstream wiring, and BYPASS may be used for noise reduction if desired. This module owns the high-current speaker drive domain, so output return paths and supply decoupling should be arranged to reduce interaction with the low-level preamp section.",
        "id": "power_amp_stage"
